---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Method | Slop Editorial" description="How the sample site is built and what its automated gates check." page="about">
  <article class="piece">
    <p class="label">Method</p>
    <h1>What the build refuses to ship</h1>
    <div class="body">
      <p>This site is a static build. Before it can be deployed, a gate script reads every generated page and fails the build on any violation.</p>
      <h2>Voice</h2>
      <p>No em dashes, no semicolons, and no contractions in visible prose. The rule is mechanical so that it never depends on a reviewer being tired.</p>
      <h2>Honesty</h2>
      <p>Every piece page must carry the sample notice. A page that loses it fails the build.</p>
      <h2>Speed</h2>
      <p>Critical CSS is inlined, no third-party host is contacted, and the JavaScript budget is small. A service worker caches repeat visits. A hover-intent queue fetches the next page before the click.</p>
      <h2>Care</h2>
      <p>Reduced motion is applied before first paint. Every image has alt text. Every internal link must resolve to a built file.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
